# Relune — Environment template

Copy to `.env` for local development.

## Core
```bash
# Local SQLite
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"

# Production Postgres example:
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://relune:relune@localhost:5432/relune?schema=public"

AUTH_SECRET="replace-with-a-long-random-string-min-32-chars"
AUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"
NEXTAUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"
PORT=3000
NODE_ENV=development
```

## OAuth (optional — leave blank to hide providers)
```bash
AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=
AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=
AUTH_GITHUB_ID=
AUTH_GITHUB_SECRET=
AUTH_APPLE_ID=
AUTH_APPLE_SECRET=
AUTH_MICROSOFT_ENTRA_ID=
AUTH_MICROSOFT_ENTRA_SECRET=
# AUTH_MICROSOFT_ID=   # alias also accepted by auth module
```

## Cache / realtime
```bash
REDIS_URL="redis://localhost:6379"
```

## Email
```bash
MAIL_PROVIDER=log
# MAIL_PROVIDER=resend
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# MAIL_FROM="Relune <noreply@yourdomain.com>"
```

## Analytics (client)
```bash
NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=none
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=console
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=plausible
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_DOMAIN=yourdomain.com
```

## PWA
```bash
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PWA=false
```

## Media (optional CDN)
```bash
# CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
# CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=
# CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=
# UPLOADTHING_TOKEN=
```
